        "original_id": "13fa119a-2dac-578b-b461-38e562a0f964",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Center for Environmental Philosophy, Alliance for Wild Ethics\n- Places: University of North Texas, Denton, Texas\n- Publications: Environmental Ethics, Nature and Madness, The Spell of the Sensuous, Orion, Parabola, Tikkun, The Ecologist\n- People: Eugene Hargrove, David Abram, Paul Shepard\n- Topics: Ecopsychology, environmental philosophy\n\nFacts:\n- In 1982, Paul Shepard published the book \"Nature and Madness,\" which ecopsychology later regarded as especially formative for the field.\n- In 1996, David Abram published \"The Spell of the Sensuous: Perception and Language in a More-than-Human World,\" and ecopsychology regarded it as especially formative for the field.\n- The Center for Environmental Philosophy is located at the University of North Texas in Denton, Texas.\n- Eugene Hargrove is the editor-in-chief of the journal \"Environmental Ethics.\"\n- The journal \"Environmental Ethics\" is published by the Center for Environmental Philosophy at the University of North Texas.\n- David Abram is the founder and creative director of the Alliance for Wild Ethics.\n- David Abram's essays on ecological disarray have appeared in journals including \"Environmental Ethics,\" \"Orion,\" \"Parabola,\" \"Tikkun,\" and \"The Ecologist.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
